# Draft knowledge entry: open62541 Windows host OHOS cross validation

id: DRAFT-open62541-ohos-windows-cross-toolchain-1.5.6
trigger_tool: conan|cmake|ninja|clang|llvm-readelf
phase: configuration|compilation|linking|testing
error_signature: CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME.*OHOS|cross-building.*runtime execution skipped|ELF 64-bit.*AArch64
severity: 2
category: toolchain|cmake|conan|cross-build|open62541
match_keywords: open62541, OHOS, armv8, aarch64, CMakeToolchain, Ninja, DevEco Native SDK, cross_building, llvm-readelf
title: open62541 Windows preflight needs an explicit OHOS host profile and target-architecture check
root_cause: >
  A Windows host can silently build with its native compiler or architecture if
  Conan host/build contexts are not separated. A recipe that only passes syntax
  checks may then produce a host artifact instead of an OHOS AArch64 package.
affected_scope: >
  C/C++ Conan recipes cross-built from Windows for HarmonyOS PC, especially
  recipes whose test_package contains an executable consumer.
verification_cmd: >
  conan create archives/o/open62541/1.5.6 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
  -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing;
  llvm-readelf -h <consumer> | findstr /i "Class Machine";
  run the consumer only in OHOS shadow CI.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: explicit-ohos-host-profile
rec_description: >
  Use os=OHOS, arch=armv8, an OHOS CMake toolchain, OHOS Clang, and Ninja in
  the host profile. Keep build tools in the build context. In test_package use
  cross_building(self) to compile/link but skip Windows execution.
rec_command: >
  conan create archives/o/open62541/1.5.6 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
  -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: ohos-profile-and-target-elf-audit
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: inspect-target-elf
fallback_description: >
  If the build succeeds but target identity is uncertain, inspect the consumer
  ELF header and generated CMake cache before changing source code.
fallback_command: llvm-readelf -h <consumer>; rg -n "CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME|CMAKE_C_COMPILER" build
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: target-architecture-audit
forbid_1_pattern: execute an AArch64 OHOS consumer on the Windows host
forbid_1_reason: The host cannot validate target runtime behavior and may report a misleading execution failure.
forbid_1_consequence: Cross-build and runtime results become conflated.
forbid_2_pattern: hardcode a developer-specific SDK path in conanfile.py
forbid_2_reason: The recipe must be reproducible on CI and other worker machines.
forbid_2_consequence: The package passes only on one workstation and cannot be submitted reliably.
principles: host-build-separation, target-elf-verification, cross-test-boundary
